# Git Push Before Deploy

**Every change must be committed and pushed to `origin` before any deploy step is run.**

## Required Order

1. Stage and commit all changes
2. Push to the remote (`git push origin <branch>`)
3. Only then run the deploy command

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT
git add .
git commit -m "your message"
git push origin main
# ...then deploy

# ❌ WRONG — never deploy without pushing first
npm run deploy   # without a prior git push
vercel           # without a prior git push
```

## Rules

- Never run a deploy command if there are unpushed commits (`git status` should show "Your branch is up to date").
- If there are uncommitted changes, commit them before pushing.
- The remote repository is: https://github.com/izzwgg-arch/bvisible.git
